      "message": "Note that as far as I could tell, builds added here eventually end up executing on chromium-swarm-dev (which surprised me, since it \"crosses\" universes between LUCI prod and LUCI dev). It works without glitches only because Skia Task Scheduler acts as a mediator between prod Buildbucket and dev Swarming. Doing this sort of stuff using native Buildbucket functionality would have required hacks.\n\nEither way it appears skia.testing doesn\u0027t need any swarming-releated ACL configuration in LUCI prod environment, thus I put them all into skia.primary.\n\nAnother option to structure this would be to define a dedicated luci.realm(...) for Swarming ACLs (e.g. \"skia.prod\") and leave skia.primary as is. Let me know if you prefer that.",
